Preserve facts through circular morphism graphs

Close strongly connected morphism components to a fixed point so
cycles and self-morphisms can transport facts. Retain owned facts
within cycles, including nested graphs, so rebuilding shared indices
cannot erase their only support. Keep single-pass propagation between
components. Preserve owned support when canonicalizing aliases already
visible by inheritance.

Exercise repeated closure, late facts, partial maps, and equalities
in native and desugared evaluation.
